      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CINQUE STELLE (8) continues to work through the grades, scoring as a $1.55 favourite before the break in a 1MW race. This is tougher, but the ratings she's running show she's up to this level, if not better. She's an exciting mare on resumption and she can continue her winning streak. LIKE CLOCKWORK (9) won well on resumption as a $1.60 pop before bumping into Bassett Hound last start when back to 1000m. Back up to 1200m is a big tick for her, though she has drawn tricky out wide. May need some luck in the early stages, but she's a lively type who can go one better. TIMELESS GEM (7) wasn't far away fresh before a 3.6L defeat behind Rock Fest last start where he held his own. Third-up now and he has the platform to improve. Worth keeping onside. SEPTEMBER BORN (2) is yet to live up to his high expectations, though he's now a gelding and the glue-on shoes being removed is a massive tick. He can start putting it all together now. HORCRUX (4) will give some cheek up front.",
